# Everything real in this folder stays out of git; the code that produces it does not.
#   fixtures/  recorded VLM extractions, Oracle tapes and engine payloads  = real invoice data
#   live/      canvas dumps + backups + execution data (contains ORDS/paperless/LLM tokens)
#   dist/      rebuilt by build.mjs / build_n8n_inline.mjs from src_*.js + standard.json
fixtures/
live/
dist/
node_modules/
__pycache__/

# ... and the files that CARRY credentials, which live outside live/:
#   n8n_nodes/port_config.json  live Keycloak bearer token (committed template: port_config.example.json)
#   nodes/                      canvas dump of node 00 (paperless token, LLM key)
#   blackbox.json               whole-workflow dump: node 00 secrets + real invoice payloads
#   parent_dump.json            parent workflow dump: node 00 secrets
# A '#' only starts a comment at the beginning of a line - a trailing comment becomes part of the pattern
# and silently stops the rule from matching, which is how this block first shipped and matched nothing.
n8n_nodes/port_config.json
nodes/
blackbox.json
parent_dump.json

# Scratch from debugging sessions (an MCP argument, a curl body, a one-off probe image). They are not
# evidence: `live/` holds the real canvas/execution dumps, and the tests rebuild whatever they need.
_*.json
_*.txt

# ---- secret hygiene (28 Oct): raw canvas dumps and built nodes carry instance credentials -------
# Every file below contains, verbatim, the paperless API token, the LiteLLM key and the ORDS bearer token
# (either as node 00 assignments or embedded in node 21's jsCode). They are working artifacts on this disk;
# none of them has ever been committed (git log -- engine/tools/n8n_port = 0 commits, 0 tracked files), and
# these rules make sure a future `git add engine/tools/n8n_port` cannot put them into version history.
live/
nodes/
blackbox.json
parent_dump.json
dist/
n8n_nodes/port_config.json
harness/py_full.py
# artifacts that ARE meant to be shared are written redacted by harness/secret_guard.py and live in workflow/
